.TH "NUSPELL" "1" "2024\-07\-03" "Nuspell 5.1.8" "User Commands"
.SH "نام (NAME)"
nuspell \- Command\-line tool for spellchecking.
.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
\f[B]nuspell\f[R] [\f[B]\-d\f[R] \f[I]dict_NAME\f[R]]
[\f[I]OPTION\f[R]]\&...
[\f[I]FILE\f[R]]\&...
.PD 0
.P
.PD
\f[B]nuspell\f[R] \f[B]\-D|\-\-help|\-\-version\f[R]
.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
Check spelling of each \f[I]FILE\f[R].
If no \f[I]FILE\f[R] is specified, check standard input.
The text in the input is first segmented into words with an algorithm
that recognizes punctuation and then each word is checked.
.SH "گزینه‌ها (OPTIONS)"
.TP
\f[B]\-d, \-\-dictionary=\f[R]\f[I]di_CT\f[R]
Use \f[I]di_CT\f[R] dictionary.
Only one is supported.
A dictionary consists of two files with extensions .dic and .aff.
The \f[B]\-d\f[R] option accepts either dictionary name without filename
extension, usually a language tag, or a path (with slash) to the .aff
file including the filename extension.
When just a name is given, it will be searched among the list of
dictionaries in the default directories (see option \f[B]\-D\f[R]).
When a path to .aff is given, only the dictionary under the path is
considered.
When \f[B]\-d\f[R] is not present, the CLI tools tries to load a
dictionary using the language tag from the active locale.
.TP
\f[B]\-D, \-\-list\-dictionaries\f[R]
Print search paths and available dictionaries and exit.
.TP
\f[B]\-\-encoding=\f[R]\f[I]ENC\f[R]
Set both input and output encoding.
.TP
\f[B]\-\-input\-encoding=\f[R]\f[I]ENC\f[R]
Set input encoding, default is active locale.
.TP
\f[B]\-\-output\-encoding=\f[R]\f[I]ENC\f[R]
Set output encoding, default is active locale.
.TP
\f[B]\-\-help\f[R]
Print short help.
.TP
\f[B]\-\-version\f[R]
Print version number.
.SH "وضعیت خروج (EXIT STATUS)"
Returns error if the argument syntax is invalid, if the dictionary can
not be loaded or if some input file can not be opened.
Otherwise, spell checking has occurred and returns success.
.SH "محیط (ENVIRONMENT)"
.TP
\f[B]DICTIONARY\f[R]
Specify dictionary, same as option \f[B]\-d\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]DICPATH\f[R]
Path to additional directory to search for dictionaries.
.SH "هشدارها (CAVEATS)"
The CLI tool is primarily intended to be used interactively by human.
The input is plain text and the output is mostly plain text with some
symbols and words that are meant to be read by human and not by machine.
The format of the output is not strictly defined and may change, thus it
is not machine\-readable.
Other programs should use the C++ library directly which has stable API.
.SH "مثال‌ها (EXAMPLES)"
.IP
.EX
nuspell \-d en_US file.txt
nuspell \-d ../../subdir/di_CT.aff
.EE
.SH "گزارش باگ‌ها (REPORTING BUGS)"
